{
  "_comment": [
    "Expected storage layout for backend/data/acceptance_worlds.",
    "This file is deliberately OUTSIDE the movable tree: nothing under",
    "backend/data/acceptance_worlds is ever trusted as configuration, because",
    "that tree is what gets moved. backend/data/ is gitignored, so config",
    "cannot live there either.",
    "",
    "layout:",
    "  local          - worlds root is a real directory on the internal disk (current state)",
    "  drive_symlink  - worlds root must be a symlink into the volume below",
    "",
    "Flip local -> drive_symlink only AFTER the symlink is in place. The guard",
    "rejects a plain local directory while drive_symlink is configured, which is",
    "what stops a launcher from silently mkdir-ing a fresh empty world when the",
    "drive is absent.",
    "",
    "Enable with: python -m core.world_storage_guard check"
  ],
  "enabled": true,
  "layout": "local",
  "worlds": {
    "root": "data/acceptance_worlds",
    "link_target": "/Volumes/Seagate Portable Drive/projects/atom/backend/data/acceptance_worlds"
  },
  "volume": {
    "mount_point": "/Volumes/Seagate Portable Drive",
    "name": "Seagate Portable Drive",
    "uuid": "0C0C11D3-8011-4F04-A213-E3EFE642C992"
  },
  "symlink_sample": 25,
  "fail_on_broken_symlinks": false
}
